Title: How to save an int value to a foreign key 
Description: In the `Post` table, there is a one-to-one foreign key on `user_id` which links to the table `Members`, there is no problem with fetching the data like this:

`[{ "post_id":1,"user_id":{"user_name":'Someone','user_id':4}, 'comment':'xxxxxx'}]`

Suppose someone makes a comment, I get his comment and user id from express session, and want to save it to the `Post` table. Since `user_id` uses `Members` type, how can I save an int value to it? 
Would you please suggest a solution?

Here's an example:

````
@Table()
export class Post {
    @PrimaryGeneratedColumn()
    post_id: number;

    @OneToOne(type => Members,entity=>entity.user_id,{
        cascadeRemove: true
    })
    @JoinColumn()
    user_id: Members;

    @Column()
    comment:string;
}

export class Members {
    @PrimaryGeneratedColumn()
    user_id: number;

    @Column()
    user_name:string;
}
````

````
    let post = new Post()
    post.comment = "sadsadsa"
    post.user_id = 44 <<=== type error!
````



